    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Thanks for recording this @gmarkall. If I have time to do this, how would you recommend I record/set an optional variable to change between the two methods? Would it be best to have it in the definition of the function (i.e. cuda.atomic.min(args..., nan_arg = True)) and pass in an additional argument to the llvm ir function? It looks like the llvm_to_ptx function in nvvm.py looks for references in the llvm ir to do a string replace with the reduction ptx so the python arguments are lost at this point. I could either add in a bool argument to the llvm ir (so the choosing is done during evaluation in CUDA kernel) or I could record the python argument in Python somewhere and pick which version to compile.\r\n",
