    "body": "@uchytilc Thanks for your interest in this - as @stuartarchibald suggests, it would probably be better to bring back the old versions with names `cuda.atomic.nanmax` and `cuda.atomic.nanmin` instead - this will avoid dealing with the additional argument. if you copy the existing parts of the implementation for `max` and `min` (the typing in `numba.cuda.cudadecl`, lowering in `numba.cuda.cudaimpl`, and the IR in `numba.cuda.cudadrv.nvvm`) and modify the IR string to implement the old behaviour, that should work - does this give you enough to go on to start implementation?",
