    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi All, thanks for taking a look at this!\r\n\r\nAfter doing a bit of investigation into https://github.com/holoviz/datashader/issues/932, I just wanted to pass along the implications of this situation for Datashader.\r\n\r\n - The change in semantics for `numba.cuda.atomic.min`/`max` in numba 0.50 was a breaking change for Datashader's GPU support (brief description in https://github.com/holoviz/datashader/issues/932#issuecomment-651395153).\r\n - In combination with https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/5746, this means Datashader will need to remain pinned to `numba<=0.48` until it's possible to get the old behavior back.\r\n - Transitively, this means that Datashader can't be compatible with the cudf/rapids 0.14+ because these have a lower bound on numba of 0.49.\r\n\r\nThanks again!",
    "created_at": "2020-06-29T22:26:09Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/5820#issuecomment-651402266",
