  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "@jonmmease There was a bug in the old semantics - the old value in the array was always supposed to be returned by `min` and `max` - however, if there was a NaN initially, then the new value got returned instead. Ideally when we implement the old behaviour again as `nanmin` and `nanmax`, we'd like to fix this bug, and ensure that the old value is always returned. Was this a behaviour that you relied on in Datashader?",
    "created_at": "2020-07-22T09:26:33Z",
